robe 4 shows `qualname=_recording_common_lock`). Autospec sees the first parameter\n  1060\t   annotated `'MergeEngine'` (a string). Check no focused test asserts on `__qualname__`/`__module__` of these methods\n  1061\t   and nothing pickles them (session-1 Codex review raised pickling; state it in the debt/changelog this time).\n  1062\t4. **Import pruning / external API.** 19 names are pruned from `_merge_engine.py` over 11 clusters (`Callable`,\n  1063\t   `Iterator`, `Outcome`, `Policy`, `Sequence`, `_observe_current_merge_candidate`, `_persist_deferred_mutation_result`,\n  1064\t   `base64`, `copy`, `dataclasses`, `os`, `prepare_merge_admission`, `re`, `runtime`, `secrets`, `sha256_bytes`,\n  1065\t   `socket`, `stat`, `sys`). Through-module readers: **0**. Apart from config, the FR-230 manifest and the spec, the only\n  1066\t   code naming the module path is `app/__init__.py:36` and `app/_dispatch.py:4` (both import only `MergeEngine`) plus the\n  1067\t   27 new `TYPE_CHECKING` imports; there is no string patch target, `sys.modules` lookup or `importlib` call on it. `CLI.<name>` reads resolve\n  1068\t   through `cli.py`'s own imports and the façade, which takes only `MergeEngine` from `_merge_engine`. The 4\n  1069\t   `patch_app`/`patch_engine`/`patch_chain_core` sites naming a pruned name are **excluded by construction**: they patch\n  1070\t   the package root plus every submodule that binds the name via `pkgutil`, never through `_merge_engine`; the new\n    68\t  (75 annotations across 27 modules; the `TYPE_CHECKING` import of `MergeEngine` makes the bare name safe), so no\n    69\t  measured per-module entry carries UP037.\n    70\t- **Unannotated tier-2 helpers and long call lines.** rope emits the helper signature and the replacement call\n    71\t  without annotations and on one line: the three `_engine_*_steps.py` modules and several in-module helpers trip\n    72\t  `E501` (and `PLR0913` where a helper has six parameters). Carried in the measured